0016:     asymmetric under all 7 non-identity dihedral transformations (ensures unique orientation match)
0017:   output: the crop rotated/reflected so internal markers match external marker layout
0018:   colors: exactly 6 distinct values (bg + base + 3 markers + 1 pattern), all from 0-9
0019: 
0020: generation_strategy:
0021:   approach: output-first
0022:   steps:
0023:     1. Pick crop dims H x W (9-13 x 9-10, not both equal unless pattern breaks symmetry).
0024:     2. Fill crop with base color 1. Choose 3 of 4 near-corner slots; assign 3 distinct marker colors.
0025:     3. Place 9-15 pixels of an internal pattern color, not touching crop border, ensuring the
0026:        full crop is asymmetric under all 7 non-identity dihedral transforms.
0027:     4. Choose a random dihedral orientation for the crop; that oriented crop is the output.
0028:     5. Compute external marker normalized positions by reading marker positions from the output.
0029:     6. Place external markers at those normalized positions offset to an empty region of the grid,
0030:        >=4 Chebyshev distance from the rectangle, occupying 3 of 4 corners of their bounding box.
0031:     7. Place the original (pre-orientation) crop on the bg=0 grid with >=1 cell gap to all edges,
0032:        ensuring the external markers also fit. Grid size 19-23 x 19-30.

===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/spce_dis/arc2_eval/62593bfd_spec.yaml =====
0001: spec:
0002:   grid: 19-30 rows x 19-30 cols
0003:   bg: most common color (varies across examples)
0004:   objects:
0005:     count: 4-6 monochromatic 8-connected components on bg
0006:     each_color: non-bg; colors usually distinct per object, but same color on different objects allowed
0007:     area: 3-12 pixels per object
0008:     bbox: 2-5 rows x 2-5 cols
0009:     shape: irregular (L, T, cross, etc.), single 8-connected component
0010:   shape_grouping:
0011:     rule: count how many objects share the same binary shape up to rotation/flip
0012:     duplicated: shape occurring >=2 times → objects move to TOP (row 0)
0013:     unique: shape occurring exactly 1 time → objects move to BOTTOM (row H-h)
0014:     note: equal area alone does not matter; only shape equivalence matters
0015:     constraint: must have >=1 duplicated shape group AND >=1 unique shape
0016:   transformation:
0017:     vertical_only: each object translated vertically; c0 preserved
0018:     top: dest_r0 = 0
0019:     bottom: dest_r0 = H - object_bbox_height
0020:   output_constraints:
0021:     no_overlap: objects must not overlap after placement at top/bottom
0022:     sufficient_gap: grid tall enough that top objects and bottom objects don't collide
0023: 
0024: generation_strategy:
0025:   approach: output-first, then scatter to get input
0026:   steps:
0027:     1. Pick H, W in [19, 30]
0028:     2. Choose 4-6 objects; create >=1 duplicated shape group and >=1 unique shape
0029:     3. For each template, grow a random 8-connected shape of area 3-12 within a 2-5 x 2-5 bbox
0030:     4. Duplicate-group members are copies of a template under random rotation/flip; singleton shapes must not match any other shape up to rotation/flip
0031:     5. Assign each object a distinct non-bg color (reuse allowed if needed for >9 objects)
0032:     6. Place duplicated-shape objects at row 0 and unique-shape objects at row H-h in the output grid
0033:     7. Ensure no pixel overlap among all placed objects
0034:     8. Build input by moving each object to a random row in the interior, preserving c0
0035:     9. Validate main(input) == output

===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/spce_dis/arc2_train/6350f1f4_spec.yaml =====
0001: spec:
0002:   grid: NxN square blocks separated by single black (0) rows/cols; N in 2-4, block_size in 2-4; total grid side = N*block_size + (N-1)
0003:   colors:
0004:     separator: 0 (black)
0005:     erased: 5 (grey) -- wildcards overlaid on blocks and separators
0006:     payload: exactly 2 distinct non-{0,5} colors; one is foreground (majority in sprite), other is blank_color (minority)
0007:   sprite: a block_size x block_size tile using both payload colors; foreground fills 67-75% of cells; no LR/UD/180 symmetry [observed]; counts of two colors must differ
0008:   block_states: each NxN macro-cell is either sprite (copy of the sprite tile) or blank (solid blank_color); sprite blocks >= blank blocks [observed]
0009:   grey_overlay: a contiguous-ish blob of grey pixels (1-2 connected components considering separators as passable) replaces some sprite/blank/separator cells; 0-25% of total pixels; each block retains >= 1 non-grey cell so its state (sprite vs blank) is unambiguous
0010:   at_least_one_clean_sprite: >= 1 block has no grey and contains the full two-color sprite (needed to infer sprite)
0011:   output: same grid size; separator lines become all-black; sprite blocks become solid foreground; blank blocks become the sprite tile; no grey remains
0012: 
0013: generation_strategy:
0014:   approach: output-first
0015:   steps:
0016:     1. Pick N (2-4) and block_size (2-4). Compute grid side = N*block_size + (N-1).
0017:     2. Pick two payload colors (not 0 or 5).
0018:     3. Generate a random block_size x block_size sprite using both colors, foreground filling 67-75% of cells, counts distinct, no all-one-color rows/cols [observed].
0019:     4. Build the NxN block state map (sprite or blank for each macro-cell). Ensure >= 1 sprite and >= 1 blank.
0020:     5. Construct the output grid: sprite blocks -> solid foreground, blank blocks -> sprite tile, separators -> black.
0021:     6. Construct the clean input grid (before grey): sprite blocks -> sprite tile, blank blocks -> solid blank_color, separators -> black.
0022:     7. Generate a grey blob: pick a random seed cell, grow via BFS/random-walk across the grid (crossing separators), replacing cells with grey (5). Ensure each block keeps >= 1 non-grey cell and remains unambiguous. Ensure >= 1 block stays fully clean with 2 colors (a sprite block). Grey covers 5-25% of grid.


